                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Rack chooser, the chain as chips, the level and whether it is in the mix at all. A boolean inside a stack of segmented rows stays segmented; a boolean in a list row is a switch \u2014 which is why the master face\u2019s per-output booleans are switches and \u201cin the mix\u201d is not. \u201cHear while playing\u201d is input-only: the tri-state exists for auto, which resolves against the record arm, and only a hardware input can be armed \u2014 the row is omitted on loop, track and master. The chain caption carries the chain\u2019s own power (\u201cChain on\u201d \/ \u201cChain off\u201d, the consequence sentence in warning beside it while off \u2014 without the pill, a chain switched off by a pedal could never be switched back on) and \u201cRe-sync from input\u201d, offered only while the routed input has an audible chain to copy. An overdub taken against a since-edited input chain shows the mismatch note above the chain: it is captured dry and does not re-inherit."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-55ea1d0f-da97-4707-a8aa-51a6f1855ee9",
